# Layer-efficiency thresholds for the review gate.
#
# Calibrated 2026-08-11 against the images here, which measured 96.6% to 99.4% efficient with 0.6 MB
# to 12 MB wasted. The floors sit just below the least efficient target measured then, so a gross
# regression (an unpruned build dependency, a forgotten cache) fails while the known waste passes. A
# change that widens waste past these bounds is a signal to prune the RUN, not to loosen a threshold.
#
# Five targets are held to .dive-ci-shadowed instead, because their waste is a base layer this
# repository did not author and cannot prune. The Makefile names which ones, and that file carries
# the reason. Nothing else is exempt, and this file stays at the numbers above.
rules:
  # Unique bytes over total bytes.
  lowestEfficiency: 0.95

  highestWastedBytes: 20MB

  # Wasted space as a fraction of the bytes the build itself added.
  highestUserWastedPercent: 0.10
